    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nA structured address form on `POST /api/owners` (and the update path), preferring structured fields while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 `OwnerFields` schema\n- Added `addressLine1` (min 1 / max 255) and optional `addressLine2` properties.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list (structured owners omit it); documented `address` as the composed output value.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**\n- Added persisted `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields with getters/setters so they round-trip through `GET`.\n\n**DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`)\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to the `owners` table.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `normalizeAddress` now normalizes `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and the flat `address` (each via `AddressNormalizer`), and derives the stored/returned flat `address` via a new `composedAddress` helper: when `addressLine1` is present it is `addressLine1` + `\" \" + addressLine2` (only when `addressLine2` is present), otherwise the normalized flat `address`.\n- `rejectBlankOwnerFields` now treats an owner as having an address when **either** a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a flat `address` is supplied (plus `city`).\n- The update path also normalizes and stamps the structured fields, keeping the composed `address` consistent.\n\nEverything downstream (household hash, postcode validation, locality) already keys off `city`/`postcode`, which are shared top-level fields in both forms, and off the composed `address` \u2014 so those continue to read the effective address.\n\n### Result\n```\nTests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreNormalizesAndComposesStructuredAddress`, `functionalityStillAcceptsFlatAddress`) pass \u2014 e.g. `addressLine1: \"10 king st\"` \u2192 returned `addressLine1: \"10 KING STREET\"` and composed `address: \"10 KING STREET\"`, and the flat-address payload is still accepted.",
